<main class="info-page"><div class="info-inner info-legal">
<h1>Privacy notice for the demo</h1><p class="info-sub">Updated October 1, 2026 · Describes the current demonstration app.</p>
<section class="info-section" id="stored-information"><h2>What the app stores</h2><p>Registration stores your name, email and optional phone number, plus a hash of your password. The app also stores demo accounts, account nicknames, simulated transactions, card records, notifications and an audit history of account actions. Recovery codes are stored as hashes; their readable values are shown only when generated.</p></section>
<section class="info-section" id="sign-in-records"><h2>Sign-in and browser storage</h2><p>A session cookie keeps you signed in. Server-side session records include a sign-in time and browser/device information for newer sessions. Successful sign-ins record the request IP address and browser information in the audit log. Individual sign-out records retain a hashed session identifier to reject a revoked session. The theme preference is saved in your browser’s local storage.</p></section>
<section class="info-section" id="data-use"><h2>How the information is used</h2><p>These records support sign-in, account settings, simulated banking activity, recovery and session management. The app’s operator can access its stored data and administrative tools. Enter fictional details and do not upload real identity, payment or financial information.</p></section>
<section class="info-section" id="external-resources"><h2>External resources</h2><p>Some pages load fonts from Google Fonts and supporting photographs from Unsplash. Your browser contacts those providers when loading their resources, which can disclose your IP address and request information. The hero photographs are served with the app. No email recovery or contact-message delivery service is connected.</p></section>
<section class="info-section" id="storage-retention"><h2>Storage and retention</h2><p>Account and activity records are stored in the app’s database, with sessions in a separate server-side store. Records can persist across server restarts and backups. No automatic account-data retention period is configured; expiration of a session does not erase account or audit records. HTTPS depends on the hosting setup; the local HTTP preview does not encrypt network traffic.</p></section>
<section class="info-section" id="account-controls"><h2>Your available controls</h2><p>In <a href="/settings">Settings</a>, you can edit your name and phone, change your password, replace recovery codes and sign out other sessions. The <a href="/security">Security page</a> lets you review sign-ins and end an individual other session. There is no self-service full-data export or account-deletion request form. Contact the person operating your demo instance for data-handling questions; the sample contact page does not send messages.</p></section>
</div></main><%- include('partials/public-footer') %></body></html>
